  <PMP_PersonaRipscanner.label>TODO</PMP_PersonaRipscanner.label>
  <!-- EN: A heavy-duty scanner unit fitted with a wide range neuro-disassembly ring and a densely packed grid of tissue probe injectors.\n\nThis upgraded scanner consumes the brain of a living human subject to extract a raw neuro-psychic pattern, a machine readable blueprint of their cognitive and emotional architecture. The circular scanner ring houses the core of the disassembly system, bathing the skull in tuned radiation while thousands of microfilaments record neural decay in real time. The result is a set of data shards known as Persona Data, each a fragment of what once was a person.\n\nThe ripscanning is fatal and irreversible, since the brain is vaporized during the process.\n\nEach scan produces atleast 1 Persona Data, but depending on additional factors based on the scanned subject’s mental complexity and failure chance in the process up to 4 units worth of data can be extracted:\n\n+1 (50% chance) if the subject has 2 or more traits\n\n+1 (50% chance) if the subject has more than 3 passions\n\n+1 if the subject has 40 or more total skill levels\n\nThe resulting Persona Data can eventually be used to construct complete persona AI cores, enabling the creation or resurrection of sentient, human equivalent and personality driven mechanoids.\n\nOptionally the scanner can be set to "Engram mode", which will instead tune the scanner to produce an engram of the passions, skill levels, and traits of the occupant. No general persona data fragments will be produced in this mode. -->
